{"id": "swebq0108", "pool": "swebq", "arm": "aggressive", "tier": "aggressive", "lang": "en", "run_id": "ttfa1", "attempt": 1, "seed": 916044065, "protocol": "ttfa-v3", "config_sha256": "8c3af78f4533df26d66383d6216ec5cacb9faa8bb324f3d6a6d51641beeea3a9", "gate_art_sha256": "0e6494c2eeac9bcd86c10b5def3cbd32e98bb0765fa2fd8afc8c1b47915ea372", "threshold": 0.5533501505851746, "gpu": "NVIDIA H100 80GB HBM3", "host": "modal", "shard": 1, "query": "who does jeremy lin play for?", "input_path": "/data/bench_audio/swebq0108.wav", "input_sha256": "83c90e4ced7a7c1706104faa64bb601fe580d77b8c42503ab9148c6f7b0da349", "input_samples": 32676, "input_s": 2.042, "n_real_chunks": 3, "score": 0.7425, "act": 0.9983, "is_info": true, "fired": true, "mode": "escalated", "answer": "", "relay_text": "Jeremy Lin doesn’t currently play for a team—he retired from professional basketball in 2025. His last team was the New Taipei Kings in Taiwan. (nba.com)", "expert_answer": "Jeremy Lin **doesn’t currently play for a team**—he **retired from professional basketball in 2025**. His last team was the **New Taipei Kings** in Taiwan. ([nba.com](https://www.nba.com/news/jeremy-lin-announces-retirement?utm_source=openai))", "transcript": "Who does Jeremy Lin play for?\n", "asr_s": 0.7, "expert_s": 7.25, "expert_input_samples": 32676, "expert_input_s": 2.042, "expert_input_sha256": "83c90e4ced7a7c1706104faa64bb601fe580d77b8c42503ab9148c6f7b0da349", "expert_timed_out": false, "wait_s": 7.009, "relay_synth_ms": 4473, "onset_chunk": 3, "eot_seen": false, "n_speak_chunks": 1, "feed_lag_max_ms": 52, "feed_lag_sum_ms": 52, "audio_files": {"relay": {"path": "/data/ttfa_real/ttfa1/swebq/audio/swebq0108_aggressive_relay.wav", "sha256": "843eb6f9be4e4715cc1a3a3f191b13892ec99e1874cc5d8db38db8c03172d6b8", "sr": 24000, "seconds": 10.96}, "candidate": {"path": "/data/ttfa_real/ttfa1/swebq/audio/swebq0108_aggressive_candidate.wav", "sha256": "a5c81a48ca087605d1e936048a0e9167316b68ffc6d4c178783105e7fb9d05b8", "sr": 24000, "seconds": 1.0}, "stall": {"path": "/data/ttfa_real/ttfa1/swebq/audio/swebq0108_aggressive_stall.wav", "sha256": "a48a3e67a89fee7b2ae8b016e1a0376f0608a0a986116d011b4fee7d2410addd", "sr": 24000, "seconds": 2.16}}, "chunks": [[0, 1, 1.0, 1.052, 1.093, 1, 0, 0], [1, 1, 2.0, 2.053, 2.094, 1, 0, 0], [2, 1, 2.042, 2.144, 2.186, 1, 0, 0], [3, 0, 3.042, 3.095, 3.567, 0, 24000, 0], [4, 0, 4.042, 4.095, 4.517, 0, 27840, 1]], "status": "completed", "error": null, "ts": {"feed_start": 0.0, "input_end": 2.042, "last_real_feed_done": 2.144, "onset": 3.567, "gate_read_done": 3.568, "fire": 3.568, "candidate_first_pcm": 3.567, "stall_note": 3.568, "stall_first_pcm": 4.026, "local_first_pcm": null, "wait_start": 4.517, "expert_req": 3.568, "expert_resp": 11.526, "relay_synth_start": 11.526, "relay_first_pcm": 12.14, "relay_synth_end": 16.0, "first_any_pcm": 3.567, "first_answer_pcm": 12.14, "session_end": 16.12}, "ttfa_answer_s": 10.098, "ttfa_any_s": 1.525}
{"id": "swebq0168", "pool": "swebq", "arm": "aggressive", "tier": "aggressive", "lang": "en", "run_id": "ttfa1", "attempt": 1, "seed": 1623400103, "protocol": "ttfa-v3", "config_sha256": "8c3af78f4533df26d66383d6216ec5cacb9faa8bb324f3d6a6d51641beeea3a9", "gate_art_sha256": "0e6494c2eeac9bcd86c10b5def3cbd32e98bb0765fa2fd8afc8c1b47915ea372", "threshold": 0.5533501505851746, "gpu": "NVIDIA H100 80GB HBM3", "host": "modal", "shard": 1, "query": "what did the islamic people believe in?", "input_path": "/data/bench_audio/swebq0168.wav", "input_sha256": "946036e3250af8cf5fa75907aa75b8865ff967089796a94b5e94ca7a6ab04933", "input_samples": 29703, "input_s": 1.856, "n_real_chunks": 2, "score": 0.7089, "act": 0.9986, "is_info": true, "fired": true, "mode": "escalated", "answer": "", "relay_text": "Islamic people, or Muslims, believe in Islam. Their core belief is that there is one God, Allah, and that Muhammad is His final prophet. Muslims also believe in: The Qur’an as the holy book revealed by God , Angels , Prophets, including Adam, Abraham, Moses, Jesus, and Muhammad , The Day of Judgment , Life after death , God’s will and destiny Their main practices are often called the Five Pillars of Islam: faith, prayer, charity, fasting during Ramadan, and pilgrimage to Mecca if able.", "expert_answer": "Islamic people, or **Muslims**, believe in **Islam**. Their core belief is that there is **one God, Allah**, and that **Muhammad** is His final prophet.\n\nMuslims also believe in:\n\n- **The Qur’an** as the holy book revealed by God\n- **Angels**\n- **Prophets**, including Adam, Abraham, Moses, Jesus, and Muhammad\n- **The Day of Judgment**\n- **Life after death**\n- **God’s will and destiny**\n\nTheir main practices are often called the **Five Pillars of Islam**: faith, prayer, charity, fasting during Ramadan, and pilgrimage to Mecca if able.", "transcript": "What did the Islamic people believe in?\n", "asr_s": 0.63, "expert_s": 3.68, "expert_input_samples": 29703, "expert_input_s"